    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "One of the most important steps in evaluating the results of numerical models is viewing the output. The ability to interactively select and view subsets or specific attributes of model results greatly enhances the utility of the results and the flexibility in application. Three-dimensional data sets and data with directional information offer a particular challenge because commonly available plotting packages (such as those developed for business applications) are poorly equipped to display these data. This contribution details several tools developed by the author for the Stanford Rock Fracture Project, specifically to view the stress and displacement fields output from the boundary-element code Poly3D.",
